binary_integrity.description:
The in-integration mode verifies the hs-frpc SHA256 before running it, and that check failed:

{error}

Enter the correct `binary_sha256` in the integration options (copy the value for your architecture from the official release page), or switch to app mode. For security reasons the integration will **not** download or execute any binary without a checksum.

client_update_failed.description:
The integration auto-updated hs-frpc to {version}, but the new binary failed to start. It has been rolled back to {previous} and restarted, so the tunnel should be back.

This usually means that version is not compatible with your system (architecture / dependencies). Suggested next steps:

1. Check on the site (User Center → Tunnel → Install wizard) whether {version} ships a build for your architecture ({arch});
2. If it keeps failing, turn off "Auto-update the in-integration hs-frpc client" in the integration options and set a working `binary_sha256` manually;
3. Report the last few `[hs-frpc]` lines from the Home Assistant log to support.

client_update_no_rollback.description:
The integration auto-updated hs-frpc to {version}, but the new binary failed to start, and no previous-version backup was available to roll back to — the tunnel is currently stuck on a version that cannot start.

Manual action needed (pick one):

1. Turn off "Auto-update the in-integration hs-frpc client" in the integration options and set `binary_sha256` back to a working build for your architecture ({arch}) — see the site's install wizard or /api/v1/tunnel/release/manifest;
2. Switch to app mode (HAOS users);
3. Report the last few `[hs-frpc]` lines from the Home Assistant log to support.
